    "result_text": "All 267 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS, including the new `Cp08Tests` and the existing owner/JDBC repository tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented registration-date defaulting for owner creation. When an owner is created without a registration date, it's now set to today and returned in the response as `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a readOnly `registrationDate` field (`format: date`) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `LocalDate registrationDate` (Jackson serializes it as `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema comes from these files.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 sets the owner's registration date to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `defaultRegistrationDate` step into the create pipeline (after `build`, before `ensureUnique`) under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nMapStruct maps `registrationDate` automatically by matching field name between `Owner` and `OwnerDto`, so no mapper change was needed.",
